{
  "_about": [
    "Which methods generate_suite.py runs, and how. Edit 'paths' once per machine (see README, step A5).",
    "Paths may start with ~. Relative paths are relative to the repo root (the folder holding src/, baselines/ and vbench_eval/).",
    "Placeholders in python/code_dir/script/args: any key of 'paths' or 'settings', {drivers} (vbench_eval/drivers), and",
    "  for batch methods {job_files} (the job files of the videos in one batch, one argument each);",
    "  for per-video methods {output}, {prompt_file} (Prompt Relay's JSON for this method), {job_file}, {prompt_joined},",
    "  {image_args} (one '--image P --image_latent_index L --image_prompt TEXT' group per image, any number of images),",
    "  {global_prompt}, {local_1}, {local_2}, ..., {image_1}, {image_2}, ..., {image_latent_2}, ...",
    "runs_on: 'text' = every entry (images not used); 'first_image' = entries with an image (uses image 1);",
    "  'images' = entries with 2 or more images, one per local prompt; 'two_images' = exactly 2 images and 2 prompts.",
    "timeline: where the events sit, recorded next to each video so evaluation scores the right frames:",
    "  'wan' / 'h3' = the prompt's Prompt Relay timing on that model's latents; 'image_latents' = event k starts",
    "  where image k is placed; 'own' = the method's driver records it.",
    "batch: true = the driver loads the model once and makes many videos (--batch_size, or 'batch_size' here).",
    "parallel: 'wan' = sharded over --gpus_per_job GPUs (FSDP + Ulysses, no offloading; on 1 GPU it offloads as",
    "  'wan_offload_model' says); 'none' = always one GPU (the first of its group)."
